From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] CHROMIUM: LSM: overlayfs mounts for root in the initial namespace

The ChromiumOS LSM refuses every overlayfs mount unless the kernel is
booted with chromiumos.allow_overlayfs, which would allow them for
everyone. NickelOS runs Android in Waydroid, whose container manager
(root, on the host) layers its changes over Android's read-only system
image with overlayfs; ARM translation libraries and NVIDIA's guest stack
go into that layer. Allow overlayfs mounts by processes with CAP_SYS_ADMIN
in the initial user namespace, and keep refusing them everywhere else,
inside user namespaces in particular, where overlayfs had its privilege
escalations.

---
--- a/security/chromiumos/lsm.c
+++ b/security/chromiumos/lsm.c
@@ -92,7 +92,14 @@
 					const char *type, unsigned long flags,
 					void *data)
 {
-	if (!allow_overlayfs && type && !strcmp(type, "overlay")) {
+	/*
+	 * NickelOS: overlayfs mounts made by root in the initial user namespace
+	 * are allowed (Waydroid's container manager layers its changes over
+	 * Android's read-only image); everyone else's stay refused, inside user
+	 * namespaces too, where overlayfs had its privilege escalations.
+	 */
+	if (!allow_overlayfs && type && !strcmp(type, "overlay") &&
+	    !capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN)) {
 		report("sb_mount", path, "Overlayfs mounts prohibited");
 		pr_notice("sb_mount dev=%s type=%s flags=%#lx\n",
 			  dev_name, type, flags);
